# Sibling releases scripts/install.sh installs when nobody passes --pin or
# --latest. Each line is: name version
# Each version is a published release with an archive for all four targets.
# scripts/release-pin-check.sh asks GitHub for those archives.
# .github/sibling-pin is the list of commits CI builds for the tests. The
# two lists name the same tool at the same point in its history:
# vissue 0.25.0 is the commit sibling-pin names, so the tests and the
# install run the same vissue. claimdag 0.8.0 is that commit too. claimdag
# has later releases, 0.9.0 and 0.9.1, that sibling-pin does not reach.
# deedar 0.4.0 is the newest release at or below the sibling-pin commit.
# The commit is on a side branch that 0.5.0 and later releases do not
# contain. sibling-pin says deedar on main writes no bytes/ and no sources
# sidecar, and the tests need that commit's output, so the install stays
# on the release behind it.
# Move a line here only together with its line in sibling-pin.
vissue 0.25.0
claimdag 0.8.0
deedar 0.4.0
